The rewrite is mechanical in the common case: the first argument is a plain string literal, each `{}` / `{:spec}` hole takes the next argument, and the argument text is spliced inside the braces (`{n + 1}`, `{n:03}`). It is not safe when the literal has positional or named holes (`{0}`, `{name}`), when the counts disagree, or when an argument's text contains a `"` or a brace; those keep the message without a fix. `{{` / `}}` escapes carry over unchanged, since f-strings use the same doubling.

